\\\"https://diceify.art/blog\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":3,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Why I Built Diceify\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://diceify.art/blog/why-i-built-diceify\\\"}]}\"}}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"relative z-[2] max-w-[800px] mx-auto w-full px-6 py-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$Lc\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog\",\"className\":\"inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-[var(--text-dim)] hover:text-[var(--pink)] transition-colors mb-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"svg\",null,{\"width\":\"20\",\"height\":\"20\",\"viewBox\":\"0 0 24 24\",\"fill\":\"none\",\"stroke\":\"currentColor\",\"strokeWidth\":\"2\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"path\",null,{\"d\":\"M19 12H5M12 19l-7-7 7-7\"}]}],\"Back to Blog\"]}],[\"$\",\"article\",null,{\"className\":\"blog-article\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"header\",null,{\"className\":\"mb-8\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex flex-wrap gap-2 mb-4\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",\"Behind the Scenes\",{\"className\":\"blog-tag\",\"children\":\"Behind the Scenes\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",\"Story\",{\"className\":\"blog-tag\",\"children\":\"Story\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"h1\",null,{\"className\":\"font-syne text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-[var(--text-primary)] mb-4\",\"children\":\"Why I Built Diceify\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"flex items-center gap-4 text-sm text-[var(--text-muted)]\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":[\"By\",\" \",\"John Mikhail\"]}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"•\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"January 24, 2024\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"•\"}],[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"children\":\"5 min read\"}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"blog-content frosted-glass rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"blog-lead\",\"children\":\"It started during COVID. I wanted to make a dice portrait of Um Kulthum — the most famous Egyptian singer of all time. But when I looked for tools to help, everything I found was... frustrating.\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"children\":\"The problem with existing tools\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"None of the tools out there gave you real control. No sharpness adjustment. No proper black and white option. Just basic converters that spit out a pattern and left you to figure out the rest.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"But even when you had a decent pattern, actually building the thing was a nightmare.\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"children\":\"Losing track of everything\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Here's what would happen: you're staring at an image of your dice pattern, trying to place dice on a frame. You look down to grab a die, look back up, and... where was I? Which row? Which column? You spend more time finding your place than actually placing dice.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"And it gets worse. When you have a run of the same die — say, ten 5s in a row — you start placing them and lose count. Was that seven or eight? Better recount. This happens constantly, and it drastically slows down an already slow process.\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"children\":\"The Builder was born\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"That's when I thought: what if there was a follow-along interface? Something that shows you exactly where you are. One die at a time. No guessing, no recounting, no losing your place.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"That's the Builder. It highlights the current position, tells you which die to place, and tracks your progress. You just follow along. It makes the whole process so much easier.\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"children\":\"Two ways to build\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"I've found there are two main approaches to physically building dice art:\"}],[\"$\",\"ul\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Glue first, then dice:\"}],\" Apply glue to the base, then place each die onto the adhesive. More controlled but slower.\"]}],[\"$\",\"li\",null,{\"children\":[[\"$\",\"strong\",null,{\"children\":\"Dice first, then glue on top:\"}],\" Arrange all the dice dry, then apply glue or resin over the top. Much faster, but risky.\"]}]]}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"I tried the second method. It's tempting because it's so much quicker. But here's the catch: if your top layer isn't transparent enough, or if it forms bubbles, it can mess up your entire piece.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"That's exactly what happened to me. So if you go that route, keep a close eye on your adhesive. Test it first on a small area.\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"children\":\"I'd love to hear about your process\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Everyone builds differently. Some people have figured out tricks I've never thought of. If you've made dice art — or you're planning to — I'd genuinely love to hear how you approached it.\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"What worked? What didn't? What would you do differently next time?\"}],[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"children\":\"Watch the full process\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Here's a video of me building the Um Kulthum portrait from start to finish:\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"blog-video\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"iframe\",null,{\"src\":\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/z4UUXeYqJZw\",\"title\":\"Building a Dice Portrait with Diceify\",\"allow\":\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture\",\"allowFullScreen\":true}]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"blog-cta\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h3\",null,{\"children\":\"Ready to start?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"children\":\"Upload a photo and see what it looks like as dice art.\"}],[\"$\",\"$Lc\",null,{\"href\":\"/editor\",\"className\":\"btn-primary\",\"children\":\"Try the editor\"}]]}]]}]]}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 text-center\",\"children\":[\"$\",\"$Lc\",null,{\"href\":\"/blog\",\"className\":\"btn-secondary\",\"children\":\"← More Stories\"}]}]]}]]\n"])</script><script>self.__next_f.push([1,"e:[[\"$\",\"meta\",\"0\",{\"name\":\"viewport\",\"content\":\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1\",{\"charSet\":\"utf-8\"}],[\"$\",\"title\",\"2\",{\"children\":\"Why I Built Diceify | Diceify\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"3\",{\"name\":\"description\",\"content\":\"The story behind Diceify — a COVID project born out of frustration with existing dice art tools, and a tribute to Um Kulthum.\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"4\",{\"name\":\"author\",\"content\":\"John Mikhail\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"5\",{\"rel\":\"manifest\",\"href\":\"/manifest.json\",\"crossOrigin\":\"use-credentials\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"6\",{\"name\":\"keywords\",\"content\":\"dice art,dice portrait,dice art generator,dice mosaic,dice portrait generator,dice picture generator,dice mosaic generator,dice mosaic maker,photo to dice,dice pixel art,diy art project,dice art gift,personalized gift ideas,personalized photo gift,custom portrait gift,unique gift ideas,diy gift ideas,handmade gift ideas,personalized birthday gift,anniversary gift ideas,christmas gift ideas,gift for board game lovers\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"7\",{\"name\":\"creator\",\"content\":\"Diceify\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"8\",{\"name\":\"publisher\",\"content\":\"Diceify\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"9\",{\"name\":\"robots\",\"content\":\"index, follow\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"10\",{\"name\":\"googlebot\",\"content\":\"index, follow, max-video-preview:-1, max-image-preview:large, max-snippet:-1\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"11\",{\"rel\":\"canonical\",\"href\":\"https://diceify.art/blog/why-i-built-diceify\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"12\",{\"rel\":\"alternate\",\"hrefLang\":\"en\",\"href\":\"https://diceify.art/blog/why-i-built-diceify\"}],[\"$\",\"link\",\"13\",{\"rel\":\"alternate\",\"hrefLang\":\"x-default\",\"href\":\"https://diceify.art/blog/why-i-built-diceify\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"14\",{\"name\":\"format-detection\",\"content\":\"telephone=no, address=no, email=no\"}],[\"$\",\"meta\",\"1